    "caption_draft": "CXL Device Architecture. Host instructions arrive at the CXL port and land in a 2MB instruction buffer; the decoder turns them into micro-ops for the PNM units and for 16 PIM controllers, each driving its GDDR6-PIM channels. The inter-device communication controller and the 64KB shared buffer carry peer-to-peer traffic between devices.",
    "open_questions": [
      "Is the LD/ST unit part of the replicated per-channel column, or one shared unit per device?",
      "Should the figure name the two PIM channels each controller manages, or is 'x16' enough?"
    ],
    "_source": "assets/exemplars/figures/asplos25-100_fig5",
    "_notes": "Captured: the three-class flow legend that makes this the corpus's clearest control-data exemplar (black solid = inter-device data, blue solid = intra-device data, orange dashed = control), the x16 replication expressed once as a container multiplicity, and the two saturated blue buffers that are the only accent fills. Not captured as geometry: the ellipsis between the two drawn replicas, the exact left-to-right nesting of the PIM column pairs, and the 'PC' box's position above the decoder -- those are grid hints only. The buffers are semantically stores but the paper draws plain rectangles, so symbol='rect' overrides the cylinder default."
  },
